B.Ut=new A.e3("How do I get my team on FolioMed?","On the Wards tab, tap Set Up a Ward. You get a 5-digit code \u2014 tap Invite to share it. Colleagues tap Join a Ward and type it in.")
B.Uy=new A.e3("What do the four tabs do?","Today shows Up Next \u2014 overdue reminders, urgent notes and your jobs, most pressing first \u2014 then counts that open the full lists, and the latest notes. Patients lists everyone on your wards. Wards is where you create, join and manage wards and units. Profile holds your details and settings.")
B.UG=new A.e3("Doctor or nurse \u2014 what changes?","Both see the same patients and notes. Doctors post notes from the compose button; nurses confirm notes through the confirm sheet, which records what was done. You can switch role in Profile.")
B.a3y=s([B.Ut,B.Uy,B.UG],t.wX)
B.Un=new A.iH("Getting started",B.a3y)
B.UF=new A.e3("How do I admit a patient?","Tap the person+ button on Today or Patients. Name is the only required field; choose the ward (and unit, if your ward uses them). FolioMed gives every patient a permanent ID such as FM000123.")
B.UJ=new A.e3("How do I edit, transfer or discharge?","Open the patient and tap \u2022\u2022\u2022 in the top corner. Edit details changes the record; Transfer moves the patient \u2014 with their notes and reminders \u2014 to another ward you belong to; Discharge moves them to the Discharged list, and Readmit brings them back under the same ID.")
B.Up=new A.e3("Can I find a baby by the mother\u2019s name?","Yes. Search on the Patients tab matches the patient\u2019s name, the mother\u2019s name, bed, diagnosis, FolioMed ID and hospital ID.")
B.a_r=s([B.UF,B.UJ,B.Up],t.wX)
B.Uo=new A.iH("Patients",B.a_r)
B.Uz=new A.e3("How are hours of life worked out?","From the birth date and time entered on the patient. Age shows in hours for the first week, then days, months and years.")
B.Uv=new A.e3(u.x,"When you add a birth time, FolioMed asks whether you\u2019ll send the investigations at 48 or 72 hours and how early to remind you (8 or 12 hours). At the hour it asks the ward whether they were sent, then asks for the results.")
B.Ux=new A.e3("What do the bilirubin lines mean?","The chart plots each reading against the phototherapy and exchange lines for the baby\u2019s gestation (and, for AAP, neurotoxicity risk factors). FolioMed picks the guideline from the gestation: NICE for babies under 35 weeks, AAP 2022 from 35 weeks. This is decision support only \u2014 always confirm against the guideline and your clinical judgement.")
B.Us=new A.e3("What is the discharge checklist?","On a newborn\u2019s page, Discharge Checklist shows what\u2019s done and what isn\u2019t. FolioMed fills in the investigations, TSH, blood grouping, OAE, a bilirubin and a weight from the last 24 hours, and whether phototherapy has stopped. Staff tick Vitamin K, BCG, OPV-0, Hepatitis B, feeding, urine and meconium, counselling and follow-up. If anything is open when you discharge, FolioMed lists it first; you can still discharge.")
B.UN=new A.e3("Why does AAP ask about risk factors?",'AAP 2022 uses lower thresholds when a baby has a neurotoxicity risk factor such as haemolysis, G6PD deficiency or sepsis. Record them (or "none") under Bilirubin on the patient page; until then FolioMed won\u2019t apply AAP lines.')
B.Zh=s([B.Uz,B.Uv,B.Ux,B.Us,B.UN],t.wX)
B.Uh=new A.iH("Newborns",B.Zh)
B.UM=new A.e3("What\u2019s in the Tools tab?","Bedside calculators \u2014 fluids and GIR (with dextrose mixing), corrected age, exchange transfusion volumes, UVC/UAC and ETT, infusion rates \u2014 low blood glucose, electrolytes and anion gap, blood pressure centiles, the national vaccine schedule \u2014 and newborn scores: Apgar, Downes, Silverman-Anderson, Thompson, LATCH, New Ballard and Modified Sarnat. A finished score can be copied or added to the baby\u2019s notes. Tap Fill from a Baby to fill in weight, day of life and gestation from an admitted patient, then check each value.")
B.Uu=new A.e3("Can I rely on the numbers?","Each tool shows its formula and source. Until your unit has checked them, every tool says so at the top \u2014 confirm against your own protocol, and have a second person check drug rates.")
B.a1B=s([B.UM,B.Uu],t.wX)
B.Ug=new A.iH("Tools",B.a1B)
B.Uw=new A.e3("What is the job list?","The day\u2019s tasks for each patient, such as \u201cRepeat TSB\u201d or \u201cPaeds review\u201d, shared by the whole ward. Add one from Today (+ \u2192 New Job) or from the patient\u2019s page. Tap the circle to tick it off; FolioMed records who did it and when.")
B.UH=new A.e3("How do I give a job to someone?","When adding a job, set For to a colleague on the ward and they get a notification. Leave it as Anyone for whoever is free. On any job, tap it and choose I\u2019ll Do It or Assign To\u2026.")
B.UA=new A.e3("Where do finished and old jobs go?","Ticked jobs stay under Jobs \u2192 Done until midnight and on the patient\u2019s page for 24 hours. Jobs move with the patient on transfer and drop off the list once the patient is discharged.")
B.a50=s([B.Uw,B.UH,B.UA],t.wX)
B.Uj=new A.iH("Jobs",B.a50)
B.Ur=new A.e3("Who sees a note?","Everyone in that patient\u2019s ward, in real time. Urgent notes are highlighted and alert the team.")
